---
  x unknown filesystem property `subvolumes`
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:9:26]
  8 |     layout {
  9 |         filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
    :                          ^^^^^^^^|^^^^^^^
    :                                  `-- not part of the schema
 10 |         var-disk "sdb"
    `----
  help: `filesystem` takes only its filesystem name

  x unknown filesystem property `pool`
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:9:43]
  8 |     layout {
  9 |         filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
    :                                           ^^^^^^|^^^^^
    :                                                 `-- not part of the schema
 10 |         var-disk "sdb"
    `----
  help: `filesystem` takes only its filesystem name

  x unknown layout property `var-disk`
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:10:9]
  9 |         filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
 10 |         var-disk "sdb"
    :         ^^^^|^^^
    :             `-- not part of the schema
 11 |     }
    `----
  help: a layout accepts `filesystem`, `composefs`, `generic-image`, `admin-
        group` and `bootloader`

  x `zfs` is not a filesystem the installer formats
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:21:9]
 20 |     layout {
 21 |         filesystem "zfs"
    :         ^^^^^|^^^^
    :              `-- not a filesystem
 22 |         composefs #true
    `----
  help: the installer auto-partitions `xfs`, `ext4` and `btrfs`

  x `sealed` names no bootloader
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:8:5]
 7 | 
 8 |     layout {
   :     ^^^|^^
   :        `-- no bootloader
 9 |         filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
   `----
  help: no family answers the bootloader: `bootloader "grub2"` here, from what
        what the base component lists

  x `sealed` installs a sealed deployment onto xfs
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:8:5]
 7 | 
 8 |     layout {
   :     ^^^|^^
   :        `-- xfs has no fs-verity
 9 |         filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
   `----
  help: the `debian` family installs with the composefs backend, which needs
        fs-verity: declare `ext4` or `btrfs`, or drop `filesystem` and take
        the family's own

  x `halfway` declares half an install layout
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:20:5]
 19 | 
 20 |     layout {
    :     ^^^|^^
    :        `-- no generic-image, admin-group, bootloader
 21 |         filesystem "zfs"
    `----
  help: nothing here has measured how `arch` installs, so this image answers
        for itself: a layout naming all of `filesystem`, `composefs`,
        `generic-image`, `admin-group` and `bootloader` builds install media,
        and no layout at all builds none

  x `sealed` declares an install layout, and nothing in the image provides
  | `bootc`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:8:5]
 7 | 
 8 |     layout {
   :     ^^^|^^
   :        `-- a bootc-only node
 9 |         filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
   `----
  help: an install layout describes how bootc installs the image: use a base
        that provides `bootc`, or drop `layout`

  x `halfway` declares an install layout, and nothing in the image provides
  | `bootc`
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:20:5]
 19 | 
 20 |     layout {
    :     ^^^|^^
    :        `-- a bootc-only node
